<!-- quality_gate agent contract — start -->
## Quality Gate agent contract

Run `bundle exec quality_gate fast` after Ruby edits. Run `bundle exec quality_gate verify` before you finish a change, and `bundle exec quality_gate audit` before you merge security-sensitive work.

Fix findings before you continue editing.

- Exit 0 means the gate ran clean.
- Exit 1 means the gate reported findings and no tool failures.
- Exit 2 means the gate could not complete cleanly because of invalid input, configuration, or another tool failure.

The default fast path keeps feedback tight with a 10-second RuboCop timeout. Verify and audit keep the broader suite work on the 120-second default timeout.

<% if agent_option?(:agents) %>The Claude Code `PostToolUse` fast hook runs after native `Edit` and `Write` calls; Codex's optional patch fast hook runs after native `apply_patch` calls. Installed Claude Code hooks can run `bundle exec quality_gate verify` automatically at session end. If those hooks become unavailable, inspect `log/quality_gate_hooks.jsonl`, run `bundle install`, and reinstall them with `bundle exec quality_gate init --profile ruby --agents`.
<% end %><% if agent_option?(:codex) %>
The optional Codex patch hook runs `quality_gate fast` after native `apply_patch` calls. It checks changed Ruby files and ERB files when Herb is configured; it does not run after shell writes or other tools. Findings appear as advisory context and never roll back the completed patch. If the gate or its tools are unavailable, Codex is asked to tell you and to run `bundle exec quality_gate fast` manually. Keep the direct manual gate and CI checks as enforcement evidence.

The final Codex Stop hook still runs the full `verify` gate, including changes made by shell commands. Findings request one repair continuation; Codex reruns verification on the resumed Stop, and remaining findings are reported while allowing the turn to finish. Unavailable checks also allow the turn to finish. This full gate can add substantial latency at every Stop. The patch hook's native timeout is 30 seconds; the shipped fast RuboCop timeout is 10 seconds, and a longer project fast budget can exceed Codex's hook limit and require manual verification.

Enable these project hooks only in a trusted project. In Codex, review `.codex/hooks/quality_gate_fast.rb`, `.codex/hooks/quality_gate_verify_stop.rb`, and both generated command definitions through `/hooks`, then explicitly trust them. Review both again after hook configuration changes. Quality Gate never changes Codex trust settings. Doctor can recognize installed files, but cannot confirm trust, activation, or live execution; Codex provides no execution history for Quality Gate to inspect.

To refresh the generated Codex hooks after a Quality Gate upgrade, run `bundle exec quality_gate init --profile ruby --codex` and review both commands in `/hooks` again. If the project moves, update both absolute commands in `.codex/hooks.json` and review them again. The installer upgrades only the exact previous Stop-only configuration generated for this same project root. Resolve customized configuration or a snapshot from another location manually using the proposal printed by the installer. To remove the integration, remove both Quality Gate hook entries and scripts; remove `.codex/hooks.json` only when it contains solely generated Quality Gate configuration. Remove only the Codex-specific instructions from `AGENTS.md` when it also contains Claude guidance, or remove the Quality Gate section when Codex is its only client.
<% else %>
Other clients, including Codex, must run `bundle exec quality_gate verify` manually before you finish a change. Codex can also use `bundle exec quality_gate fast` after edits for file-scoped feedback.
<% end %>
<!-- quality_gate agent contract — end -->
